\b\f1 Artist Portfolio Website Presentation\par
\b0\f0
\par
\b 1. Introduction\par
\b0
Good day everyone. For this assignment, I created an Artist Portfolio Website from scratch for YoungPapi. The purpose of the website is to present the artist's brand, music journey, visuals, social platforms, and contact details in one complete and professional online space.\par
\par
\b 2. Planning and Structure\par
\b0
Before coding, I planned the website pages and user flow. I designed six linked pages: Home, About, Music, Gallery, Contact, and Links. This structure helped me organize content clearly and made navigation simple and consistent for users.\par
\par
\b 3. Development From Scratch\par
\b0
I used HTML to build the content and layout of every page, CSS3 in an external stylesheet to design a consistent visual theme, and JavaScript to add interactivity. I also integrated Bootstrap for responsive support and framework usage required by the rubric.\par
\par
\b 4. Key Features Implemented\par
\b0
- Consistent navigation bar across all pages with no broken internal links.\par
- Responsive design for desktop and mobile screens.\par
- Branded homepage with artist identity and call-to-action buttons.\par
- Gallery section with images that include alt text, width, and height attributes.\par
- Contact form using HTML5 validation with required fields and email validation.\par
- JavaScript behavior: mobile menu toggle, active page highlighting, dynamic footer year, and contact form success feedback.\par
\par
\b 5. Rubric Alignment\par
\b0
This website addresses the key Part B marking areas by providing:\par
- A complete and uniform page structure.\par
- Meaningful CSS selectors and an external stylesheet.\par
- Bootstrap framework integration.\par
- Functional behavior layer with validated form inputs.\par
- Accessible content elements such as alt text and semantic page sections.\par
\par
\b 6. Challenges and Solutions\par
\b0
The main challenge was maintaining consistency across multiple pages while keeping the design clean. I solved this by reusing a shared navigation/header-footer structure, centralizing styles in one CSS file, and testing links and form behavior repeatedly.\par
\par
\b 7. Conclusion\par
\b0
In conclusion, this project demonstrates my ability to plan, design, and build a multi-page website from scratch using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and Bootstrap. I improved my skills in structure, styling, responsiveness, and user-focused functionality. The final product is a polished artist portfolio ready for presentation and further deployment.\par
\par
\b Closing Line\par
\b0
Thank you for listening. I am ready to demonstrate the website and answer any questions.\par
